-- A join line's WITHIN is the deadline on the whole group (R-T2), so it IS
-- what OF THE DEADLINE names, and the group's join has not fired when it is
-- read: neither THE JOIN nor THE DEADLINE can anchor it
-- (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.1, a build decision of 2026-09-15). THE
-- ARMING — the EVERY's own arming — and an instant are the two anchors a join
-- line takes; run-anchors.l4 pins both.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) ONCE ALL HAVE WITHIN 14 OF THE JOIN HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`also bad` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) UPON EACH WITHIN 14 OF THE DEADLINE HENCE FULFILLED
